    <description>Reusable fault handler (autolaunched). Call from any fault connector: pass $Flow.FaultMessage, your flow's API name and the faulting element's name; read back a user-safe message, next steps, admin guidance, a reference ID, classification flags and a ready-made rich-text display block. Works in screen, autolaunched and record-triggered flows. For screen flows prefer FlowFaultHandlerScreen, which adds roll back and the standard error screen.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Contact-admin text used when the handler action itself fails.</description>
        <name>FallbackNextSteps</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>SUBSTITUTE({!$Label.FlowFaultNextStepsContactAdmin}, "{0}", "your Salesforce administrator")</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Original fault plus the handler's own fault, for the technical details.</description>
        <name>FallbackTechnicalMessage</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>"Flow: " &amp; {!flowApiName} &amp; " | Element: " &amp; {!elementApiName} &amp; BR() &amp; "Fault: " &amp; {!faultMessage} &amp; BR() &amp; "Handler fault: " &amp; {!$Flow.FaultMessage}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Generic user message used when the handler action itself fails.</description>
        <name>FallbackUserMessage</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>SUBSTITUTE({!$Label.FlowFaultHandlerUnavailable}, "{0}", "your Salesforce administrator")</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>FlowFaultHandlerCore {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Flow Fault Handler (Core)</label>
